  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}48 & a \\\\ a & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $a.$",
  "worked_solution": "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =48\\cdot 3-a\\cdot a \\\\  & =144-{a}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}144-{a}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =144 \\\\ a & =\\pm 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $a$ are $a=\\pm 12.$",
